    "stars": 2,
    "text": "현지화를 한 건지 한국인인 우리 입맛에는 맞지 않았음. 보쌈은 지방이 적어 퍽퍽하고 보쌈김치는 그 특유의 맛이 안 느껴지고 평범했음. 물회는… 물회인지 샐러드인지 모르겠음. 회 양이 너무 적음. 스레드에서 본 사진에는 오징어도 있던데 우리꺼에는 없었음. 제일 실망이었던 건 알밥. 언제부터 알밥이 차가운 메뉴었는지? 그냥 회덮밥에서 회 대신 알을 넣은 것 같았음. 우리가 아는 그 알밥이 아니라 포케볼 같음. 그리고 물회도 그렇고 알밥도 그렇고 묘하게 고수 비슷한 맛이 나던데.. 시소인가..? 암튼 다 못 먹고 남김.",
    "textTranslated": "Whether it was localized or not, it didn't suit our Korean palates. The bossam was dry due to low fat content, and the bossam kimchi lacked that distinctive flavor and was just average. As for the mulhoe... I couldn't tell if it was mulhoe or a salad. The amount of raw fish was far too small. The photos I saw in the thread showed squid, but ours didn't have any. The biggest disappointment was the roe rice. Since when did roe rice become a cold dish? It seemed like they just put roe in a raw fish rice bowl instead of the fish. It wasn't the roe rice we know; it was more like a poke bowl. Also, both the mulhoe and the roe rice had a strange taste similar to cilantro... Was it shiso...? Anyway, we couldn't finish it and left some behind."
  },
